WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.441 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:31.531
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:31.615 --> 00:33.951
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:34.451 --> 00:35.494
You're already out.

00:39.540 --> 00:41.333
-I'll see you around.
-[aunt] Sure.

00:43.126 --> 00:46.171
Hey, did you say
the walking trail was that way?

00:46.255 --> 00:47.297
-It is.
-Right.

00:52.261 --> 00:53.512
What about your wife?

00:53.971 --> 00:55.806
-Sorry?
-[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:57.307 --> 00:58.433
His wife?

00:59.518 --> 01:00.769
[line ringing]

01:04.856 --> 01:05.899
[phone vibrating]

01:08.360 --> 01:09.695
CACTUS

01:10.195 --> 01:11.905
[automated message plays faintly]

01:14.533 --> 01:15.784
[line ringing]

01:17.160 --> 01:18.412
[phone vibrating]

01:21.498 --> 01:22.624
[hesitates]

01:27.796 --> 01:29.590
[♪ dramatic music continues]

01:36.179 --> 01:37.347
[♪ comical sting]

01:42.227 --> 01:43.770
[♪ dramatic music playing]

01:52.362 --> 01:53.989
[♪ dramatic sting]

01:54.072 --> 01:55.574
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

02:09.338 --> 02:10.339
[Meri exclaims softly]

02:11.882 --> 02:13.383
Does he know those people?

02:14.134 --> 02:15.510
-In there--
-No way.

02:16.386 --> 02:17.387
No.

02:17.471 --> 02:19.514
No can do. I mean...

02:20.015 --> 02:21.683
I want to check out the walking trail.

02:21.767 --> 02:23.644
-Yes, but--
-But anyway.

02:23.727 --> 02:24.978
Let's go.

02:25.062 --> 02:26.438
Come along.

02:26.521 --> 02:28.273
I want to check that out now.

02:28.357 --> 02:29.358
[Sanghyeon] But...

02:29.441 --> 02:31.068
-[Kim Wooju] Right away.
-[sighs]

02:38.617 --> 02:39.743
[sucks teeth]

02:42.162 --> 02:44.164
Oh, boy. [sighs]

02:44.915 --> 02:46.124
Oh, this thing.

02:47.125 --> 02:48.460
-Did he see it?
-No.

02:48.543 --> 02:51.004
But it doesn't matter if he knows.

02:51.088 --> 02:53.215
He'll hear about it from Grandma.

02:53.298 --> 02:54.758
Still, do not say a word.

02:54.841 --> 02:56.802
What if he puts a wrench in the works?

02:56.885 --> 02:58.637
Well, yes. He could do that.

02:58.720 --> 03:01.973
Wooju seems to have something like
an inferiority complex around me.

03:02.057 --> 03:05.143
[laughs smugly] It's because I grew up
in a loving environment.

03:05.227 --> 03:07.646
Did he say his friend lives here?

03:07.729 --> 03:08.980
-Right?
-Yes.

03:09.064 --> 03:10.565
Which friend?

03:10.649 --> 03:13.193
-[GPS] It's 3:00 p.m.
-I don't know, and it's 3:00 p.m. now.

03:13.276 --> 03:14.403
Okay.

03:14.486 --> 03:16.321
MOM

03:17.239 --> 03:18.365
[phone ringing]

03:28.417 --> 03:29.668
[phone continues ringing]

03:29.751 --> 03:31.253
[car approaching]

03:33.088 --> 03:34.589
Hey, wait. Stop the car.

03:34.673 --> 03:35.799
[Eungsoo] What for?

03:35.882 --> 03:37.426
Isn't this a ringtone?

03:38.051 --> 03:39.928
-It's not mine.
-It's not mine, either.

03:41.555 --> 03:43.014
There's a phone over there.

03:43.098 --> 03:44.975
What? There's a phone out there?

03:45.058 --> 03:46.059
-Yes.
-Here.

03:47.102 --> 03:48.854
What? Why are you so nosy, Mom?

03:48.937 --> 03:50.063
You be quiet.

03:50.147 --> 03:51.398
-Mom.
-[phone continues ringing]

03:51.481 --> 03:52.607
What's wrong with her?

03:53.316 --> 03:57.237
That punk is so inconsiderate.

03:57.320 --> 03:59.197
He should help people
get their things back.

03:59.281 --> 04:00.449
Why are you so nosy?

04:00.532 --> 04:03.452
-Seriously, why?
-Oh, dear. I missed the call.

04:04.244 --> 04:05.245
Let's see.

04:06.204 --> 04:07.664
Mom, we don't have time to...

04:08.957 --> 04:11.126
-[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]
-There's no time.

04:11.209 --> 04:13.086
What got into her this time?

04:13.170 --> 04:14.254
You stay there.

04:22.971 --> 04:24.556
-[♪ dramatic sting]
-[gasps]

04:25.015 --> 04:26.224
[dog barks]

04:26.308 --> 04:27.309
What are you doing?

04:30.854 --> 04:32.606
[♪ unsettling, dramatic music playing]

04:32.689 --> 04:33.982
-[chittering]
-[gasps]

04:37.319 --> 04:38.403
[Eungsoo] What's that?

04:39.613 --> 04:41.114
[Miyeon] Oh, my. Oh, my. Oh, my...

04:41.198 --> 04:43.742
[Eungsoo] What's wrong with her?
Come here, Mom.

04:43.825 --> 04:46.161
-Mom.
-Oh, my goodness...

04:46.244 --> 04:47.704
-Oh, dear.
-Say you're sorry, Mom.

04:49.539 --> 04:51.082
-[Miyeon] Wait, what is...
-[Eungsoo] Go on.

04:51.166 --> 04:52.459
Hey.

04:52.542 --> 04:53.585
Well, this...

04:53.668 --> 04:54.795
Is this your phone?

04:54.878 --> 04:57.130
It was on the ground, so I picked it up.

04:57.214 --> 04:58.340
-Apologize, Mom.
-Is this...

04:58.423 --> 04:59.508
-Give it to her already.
-Gosh.

04:59.591 --> 05:00.634
-Sorry.
-Goodness.

05:00.717 --> 05:01.843
-Oh, dear.
-[Meri] Thank you.

05:01.927 --> 05:03.345
-I'm really sorry.
-[Meri] Thank you.

05:03.428 --> 05:04.513
Sorry.

05:06.640 --> 05:09.518
Oh, dear, she looked fine,
but she must be ill.

05:09.601 --> 05:11.394
She seemed to be mentally unstable.

05:11.478 --> 05:14.105
She doesn't seem to know
if she can talk or not, does she?

05:14.189 --> 05:16.858
There's no way someone unstable
would live in this neighborhood.

05:16.942 --> 05:18.693
-Is this place cursed or...
-[dog growls softly]

05:19.069 --> 05:20.987
Oh, look at the doggy.

05:21.363 --> 05:22.364
[gasps]

05:22.656 --> 05:23.824
That thing looks unwell, too.

05:23.907 --> 05:25.158
Hang on.

05:26.159 --> 05:27.911
[barks] It won't react.

05:27.994 --> 05:29.746
[barking]

05:29.830 --> 05:31.039
This doesn't look good.

05:31.122 --> 05:32.624
[♪ dramatic music playing]

05:32.707 --> 05:34.376
[growling]

05:34.459 --> 05:35.877
[both panicking]

05:36.878 --> 05:39.798
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

05:39.881 --> 05:41.007
EPISODE 3

05:41.091 --> 05:44.010
I told the managing director
that you'd left home already.

05:44.553 --> 05:47.556
Where did you hide earlier?
You disappeared in an instant.

05:48.348 --> 05:49.432
[dog barking]

05:51.560 --> 05:53.436
Just somewhere.
[chuckles softly]

05:53.520 --> 05:54.521
He didn't catch on, did he?

05:55.188 --> 05:56.815
No, fortunately.

05:58.108 --> 06:02.487
-So, who were those people?
-They were my relatives.

06:02.779 --> 06:03.780
[gasps]

06:03.864 --> 06:05.031
It could've gone bad for us.

06:05.115 --> 06:06.116
What did I tell you?

06:08.493 --> 06:10.829
If you stay there,
you might meet more people you know.

06:11.204 --> 06:12.289
[sighs]

06:12.372 --> 06:15.125
Fine, I won't live there. Don't worry.

06:15.208 --> 06:17.669
Did you find a place to stay?

06:17.752 --> 06:19.754
You said you had to move out
of your old place.

06:19.838 --> 06:20.964
Well...

06:21.047 --> 06:22.299
I'll start looking.

06:22.382 --> 06:25.594
Okay, all I ask of you
is that you sort things out,

06:25.677 --> 06:27.512
so I don't have to worry
about you anymore.

06:27.596 --> 06:30.098
Our deal is done here.

06:30.724 --> 06:32.934
I know when I've overstayed my welcome.

06:33.435 --> 06:34.853
I won't ask any more of you.

06:35.770 --> 06:38.273
Then, goodbye.

06:38.356 --> 06:39.399
Bye.

06:39.482 --> 06:40.692
[line disconnects]

06:42.110 --> 06:43.153
Goodness.

06:43.612 --> 06:45.113
He's so mean and unkind.

06:46.281 --> 06:47.449
But still,

06:48.408 --> 06:49.743
he did me a great favor.

06:50.869 --> 06:53.663
I have to pay back both Mom and the loan.

06:54.914 --> 06:56.333
He's a lifesaver.

06:56.416 --> 06:58.460
Yes, he saved my life.

07:06.468 --> 07:08.470
She was short of breath
early in the morning.

07:09.304 --> 07:10.930
And she feels dizzy more frequently.

07:11.765 --> 07:13.892
That's because of her blood pressure.

07:14.601 --> 07:16.227
Does she take her medication on time?

07:16.311 --> 07:17.395
Yes.

07:17.479 --> 07:18.897
I'm old, that's all.

07:18.980 --> 07:21.358
Old bodies are bound to break down.

07:21.983 --> 07:24.152
Ms. Kim, go check that for me.

07:24.694 --> 07:25.695
Sure.

07:26.696 --> 07:29.949
You need to reduce
your stress and workload.

07:30.492 --> 07:31.951
And your sodium intake.

07:32.035 --> 07:33.370
Okay, I will.

07:33.662 --> 07:35.163
[chuckles softly]

07:35.246 --> 07:38.750
Now that you're a real doctor,
you're nagging me like one.

07:38.833 --> 07:41.294
[chuckles]
She's old enough to get married.

07:41.378 --> 07:43.755
Do you have someone in mind as a suitor?

07:43.838 --> 07:46.132
She had eyes only for one
since she was a kid.

07:46.216 --> 07:47.217
Your grandson Wooju.

07:47.300 --> 07:48.760
Dad.

07:49.552 --> 07:51.096
You still like him?

07:51.179 --> 07:54.474
Why won't you do anything?
You need to drop hints like crazy.

07:54.974 --> 07:56.810
He won't know how you feel.

07:57.602 --> 07:59.312
Do you approve of me?

07:59.396 --> 08:02.482
I'd love for you
to be my granddaughter-in-law.

08:02.565 --> 08:03.566
[♪ whimsical music playing]

08:03.650 --> 08:06.903
I'll trust you've got my back
and make my move on him.

08:06.986 --> 08:09.072
Yes, give it a go.

08:10.240 --> 08:11.700
Director Yoon.

08:11.783 --> 08:13.118
We might become in-laws.

08:13.201 --> 08:15.495
How about we wrap it up this year
while we're at it?

08:15.578 --> 08:17.664
[all chuckle]

08:20.250 --> 08:22.961
MYUNGSOONDANG

08:23.044 --> 08:24.838
[♪ soft, gentle music
playing over speakers]

08:50.071 --> 08:51.614
Oh, Mr. Kim?

08:51.698 --> 08:53.742
Hey. You came in early.

08:53.825 --> 08:55.577
It's not yet time to clock in.

08:55.660 --> 08:58.455
I'm the youngest on the team,
so I need to come in early.

08:58.538 --> 09:00.123
And I love being at work.

09:00.206 --> 09:01.499
[acknowledges]

09:01.583 --> 09:02.584
What would you like?

09:02.667 --> 09:04.085
-Is it your treat?
-Yes.

09:04.169 --> 09:05.962
An iced Americano, then.

09:06.046 --> 09:10.467
One iced Americano
and another one with two extra shots.

09:11.468 --> 09:13.428
I'll pay for these as well.

09:13.511 --> 09:15.388
-Okay, is it to go?
-Yes.

09:15.472 --> 09:18.058
I'll treat you next time.
Promise to give me a chance.

09:19.350 --> 09:20.351
Okay.

09:26.483 --> 09:28.151
[Sejung] Hello, Mr. Jang.

09:28.234 --> 09:29.319
Oh, hi, Sejung.

09:29.986 --> 09:31.571
Go on your way. [in English] Good morning.

09:32.572 --> 09:33.782
-Mr. Jang?
-[in Korean] Yes?

09:33.865 --> 09:35.617
-What?
-A word?

09:36.659 --> 09:37.744
Okay.

09:39.412 --> 09:40.580
[mouthing]

09:41.664 --> 09:43.750
[sighs] You heard, didn't you?

09:44.667 --> 09:45.710
About what?

09:47.045 --> 09:48.421
[laughs]

09:48.880 --> 09:50.465
The contract.

09:50.548 --> 09:52.258
[in English] You did a good job.

09:52.342 --> 09:55.261
[in Korean] You punk. I knew you'd manage.

09:55.345 --> 09:57.263
I believed in you all along, kid.

09:57.347 --> 09:58.348
Okay?

09:59.641 --> 10:01.267
[laughs loftily]

10:01.351 --> 10:02.727
We can laugh about it.

10:02.811 --> 10:04.896
Do you need anything
from the Business Management Team?

10:04.979 --> 10:06.481
-Name it.
-Not doing anything

10:06.564 --> 10:07.649
is the best you can do.

10:07.732 --> 10:08.900
Focus on your own job.

10:12.112 --> 10:14.364
You and the design company CEO...

10:15.949 --> 10:16.950
Do you know each other?

10:18.326 --> 10:19.369
[clears throat]

10:19.452 --> 10:22.122
How would I know her?
I don't know anyone here.

10:22.205 --> 10:24.958
True. You have zero contacts here.

10:25.041 --> 10:28.419
What kind of deal did you offer
that made her sign it so easily?

10:28.503 --> 10:30.171
Can you tell me that at least?

10:30.255 --> 10:31.840
Are you upset I didn't get a bad deal?

10:32.799 --> 10:34.884
[scoffs, hesitates]

10:36.219 --> 10:37.929
Why would I be upset?

10:38.012 --> 10:40.557
What kind of skills
does my dear cousin have?

10:40.640 --> 10:43.601
I'd like to humbly learn
a few things if I could.

10:44.519 --> 10:45.812
[chuckles softly]

10:48.356 --> 10:49.732
I won't tell you.

10:49.816 --> 10:52.110
Ask her yourself if you want to know.

10:52.193 --> 10:53.486
I have to head to a meeting.

10:54.154 --> 10:56.531
[stutters] I'm not done talking, punk.

10:57.365 --> 10:58.992
I have a meeting, too, you know.

10:59.075 --> 11:00.493
You...

11:00.577 --> 11:01.578
How dare he?

11:01.661 --> 11:05.081
I wish he would trip up
just a bit on the way.

11:05.165 --> 11:06.457
[chuckling]

11:06.541 --> 11:07.584
It worked.

11:09.085 --> 11:11.671
I swear there's more to it.

11:14.132 --> 11:16.009
You have something urgent to tell me?

11:16.968 --> 11:18.887
Yes, well...

11:19.721 --> 11:21.055
It's about J Consulting,

11:21.139 --> 11:23.433
the company that's helping us
enter the US market.

11:25.518 --> 11:27.812
Yes, is there an issue with them?

11:29.063 --> 11:30.398
Could you take a look at this?

11:38.406 --> 11:39.657
FINANCIAL STATEMENT

11:39.741 --> 11:42.452
Other than the monthly consulting fee,

11:42.535 --> 11:45.997
we wire J Consulting all the funds
to build the US factory

11:46.080 --> 11:48.708
and pay the subcontractors as well.

11:49.500 --> 11:52.212
It looks like J Consulting
is embezzling some of it.

11:52.295 --> 11:53.630
[♪ gripping, tense music playing]

11:53.713 --> 11:55.840
I found it odd
and contacted our US counterpart,

11:55.924 --> 11:59.552
and the company itself seems to have
exaggerated their performance.

12:01.137 --> 12:02.138
About this.

12:02.222 --> 12:05.516
Mr. Ko, does anyone other than you
know of this?

12:05.600 --> 12:07.352
No. Right now, it's just me.

12:07.977 --> 12:10.063
You're the first person I'm alerting.

12:10.146 --> 12:11.898
That's very wise of you.

12:11.981 --> 12:13.608
Keep this confidential for now.

12:14.150 --> 12:16.778
I'll look into it as soon as I can.

12:17.654 --> 12:19.113
Yes, sir.

12:19.906 --> 12:20.949
[sighs]

12:26.829 --> 12:28.331
REALTOR

12:28.414 --> 12:31.292
[relator] I have a place
that will be available in a week.

12:31.376 --> 12:34.587
Even if it's a short-term lease,
the deposit is five million won.

12:34.963 --> 12:37.090
[sighs] I don't have five million won.

12:38.174 --> 12:41.511
[sighs deeply] The dry sauna closed down,

12:41.594 --> 12:42.804
and I have nowhere to go.

12:43.346 --> 12:44.430
[inhales deeply]

12:44.514 --> 12:47.267
My only friend who lives in Seoul...

12:49.936 --> 12:51.396
is Gyeonghwa.

12:54.107 --> 12:55.483
[line ringing]

12:56.442 --> 12:57.610
[line connects]

12:57.694 --> 13:00.863
Hey, Gyeonghwa.
How are you doing?

13:00.947 --> 13:03.408
-What's up, Meri?
-[♪ whimsical music playing]

13:03.950 --> 13:05.118
My place?

13:05.201 --> 13:07.620
Oh, you should've called
just a tad sooner.

13:07.704 --> 13:09.122
I moved out.

13:09.872 --> 13:12.000
Why else? I joined the army.

13:13.084 --> 13:14.168
Salute.

13:16.170 --> 13:18.172
[chuckles] Man, you didn't know?

13:18.256 --> 13:19.716
I enlisted last month.

13:19.799 --> 13:21.259
Are you serious?

13:22.051 --> 13:24.429
You mean you're an officer?

13:24.971 --> 13:26.973
I wouldn't know if you don't tell me.

13:27.056 --> 13:29.017
I didn't tell until I got in.

13:29.100 --> 13:30.727
It would be embarrassing if I failed.

13:31.311 --> 13:33.938
But why do you need a place
for three months?

13:34.022 --> 13:36.065
I thought you got one before the wedding.

13:36.149 --> 13:38.192
The schedule got a bit messed up.

13:39.235 --> 13:41.195
There's a thing or two.

13:42.030 --> 13:43.740
It can't be helped, then.

13:43.823 --> 13:45.867
-Is something wrong?
-Oh, no.

13:46.617 --> 13:48.327
I'll find some place else.

13:48.911 --> 13:51.497
Hey, don't worry about me and eat well.

13:51.581 --> 13:52.707
Look after yourself.

13:54.208 --> 13:56.419
[chuckles softly]
Sure, salute to you, too.

14:00.048 --> 14:01.132
[line disconnects]

14:01.716 --> 14:03.843
Gosh, what should I do now?

14:09.057 --> 14:10.850
[♪ enthralling music playing]

14:18.483 --> 14:20.193
DAEJONG MOTEL
NO DEPOSIT, LONG-TERM STAY WELCOME

14:20.985 --> 14:23.279
DAEJONG MOTEL

14:31.954 --> 14:33.873
[♪ gripping music playing]

14:38.086 --> 14:39.253
[siren wailing]

14:39.337 --> 14:40.922
DAEJONG MOTEL

14:41.005 --> 14:42.423
[couple chattering]

14:42.507 --> 14:43.966
[woman] Why did we bother coming here?

14:44.050 --> 14:45.593
-[man] Wait, I can--
-[woman] Let go of me.

14:45.676 --> 14:47.011
[man] It was the alcohol, okay?

14:47.095 --> 14:48.596
Sir, can't we get a refund?

14:48.679 --> 14:50.473
-We were here just ten minutes.
-[receptionist] No.

14:50.556 --> 14:51.849
-We don't need a refund.
-Let me go.

14:51.933 --> 14:53.518
Give me another shot.
I can do it this time.

14:53.601 --> 14:55.686
No, you couldn't even last a minute.

14:55.770 --> 14:56.813
[man] I swear.

14:58.022 --> 15:00.316
-Are you alone?
-Yes.

15:00.858 --> 15:01.859
[sniffles]

15:01.943 --> 15:04.028
You can't cook in the room.

15:04.112 --> 15:06.531
If you have dirty clothes,
leave them with the cleaning lady.

15:06.614 --> 15:07.990
-She'll charge you per kilo.
-Okay.

15:09.575 --> 15:10.576
Good night.

15:15.706 --> 15:16.999
[♪ dramatic sting]

15:22.463 --> 15:23.714
[panting]

15:25.049 --> 15:26.092
[grunts softly]

15:26.926 --> 15:27.927
[continues panting]

15:30.138 --> 15:31.305
[footsteps approaching]

15:37.812 --> 15:39.313
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

16:02.587 --> 16:03.671
[door handle rattling]

16:10.094 --> 16:11.095
[sighs in relief]

16:15.558 --> 16:16.684
[soft electrical hum]

16:33.910 --> 16:35.036
[sighs wearily]

16:36.204 --> 16:37.872
It's just for three months.

16:40.958 --> 16:42.585
This place is a mess.

16:44.503 --> 16:47.006
DO NOT BE WORRIED!
THE BEDDING HAS BEEN FRESHLY REPLACED

16:47.089 --> 16:48.716
[♪ whimsical music playing]

16:48.799 --> 16:50.468
DAEJONG MOTEL

16:50.551 --> 16:51.636
[exclaims in disgust]

16:54.096 --> 16:56.390
I doubt I can fall asleep here.

16:57.266 --> 16:58.768
[phone alarm ringing]

17:01.062 --> 17:03.064
ALARM

17:12.281 --> 17:13.950
[phone alarm continues]

17:21.499 --> 17:22.500
[alarm stops]

17:31.676 --> 17:32.677
What time is it?

17:37.682 --> 17:38.975
[♪ dramatic sting]

17:39.058 --> 17:40.059
No way.

17:40.142 --> 17:41.644
[♪ enthralling music playing]

17:52.530 --> 17:53.656
My jacket.

17:56.409 --> 17:57.410
Where is it?

18:02.957 --> 18:04.917
[sighs] My phone.

18:12.383 --> 18:13.384
The samples.

18:15.136 --> 18:16.304
What's this in my hair?

18:19.390 --> 18:20.391
Here you go.

18:21.142 --> 18:23.477
It's the safest thing to give out
as an opening souvenir.

18:24.437 --> 18:26.981
The transparent bottle
shows how much is left,

18:27.064 --> 18:30.192
and the pump is gentle enough
for kids to use it.

18:30.860 --> 18:34.071
The name of your clinic
and the logo are on the label.

18:34.155 --> 18:36.073
Isn't the logo a bit too small?

18:36.157 --> 18:40.369
I thought you'd say that,
so I prepared a sample with a bigger logo.

18:41.329 --> 18:43.497
Do you want it to be bigger or not?

18:43.581 --> 18:44.582
I think this will do.

18:44.665 --> 18:47.627
Okay, then I'll confirm the design
and move ahead.

18:47.710 --> 18:48.711
[doctor] Okay.

18:50.338 --> 18:51.922
I'll see you next time.

18:52.006 --> 18:54.050
-See you.
-[woman] Goodbye.

18:54.717 --> 18:56.135
[hesitates]

18:56.218 --> 18:57.219
Aren't you...

18:57.470 --> 18:58.888
[exclaims in realization]

18:58.971 --> 18:59.972
Hello.

19:00.598 --> 19:02.099
Hello.

19:02.183 --> 19:03.184
Are you unwell?

19:03.267 --> 19:05.144
No, I was here for work.

19:05.227 --> 19:06.646
[acknowledges]

19:06.729 --> 19:08.939
[♪ soft orchestral music playing
over speakers]

19:16.906 --> 19:18.366
[footsteps approaching]

19:23.204 --> 19:24.205
Thank you.

19:33.172 --> 19:35.675
I dropped by
because a college friend opened a clinic.

19:35.758 --> 19:37.468
-Today is my day off.
-I see.

19:39.220 --> 19:41.263
Have you healed okay?

19:41.347 --> 19:42.348
Oh, yes.

19:42.431 --> 19:45.267
You treated me so well that time.

19:45.935 --> 19:47.311
Thank you for that.

19:47.395 --> 19:49.021
Not at all.

19:49.105 --> 19:51.732
I should look out
for Wooju's acquaintances.

19:51.816 --> 19:55.277
-Hmm.
-So, was that the first time you'd met?

19:55.361 --> 19:56.570
Yes.

19:57.196 --> 20:00.074
There was a slight mishap that time.

20:00.825 --> 20:02.785
I said I was fine,

20:02.868 --> 20:05.287
but he insisted on taking me
to see a doctor.

20:06.205 --> 20:09.083
He paid for the treatment
and even took me home.

20:09.709 --> 20:11.627
I was a huge nuisance.

20:12.211 --> 20:14.964
He's known to be caring and polite.

20:15.631 --> 20:18.718
He grumbles,
but does what he can to help out.

20:19.260 --> 20:20.469
I see.

20:21.887 --> 20:25.891
It looks like you kept contacting him.

20:25.975 --> 20:28.102
He told me he saw you again,

20:28.185 --> 20:32.481
and that you were a bit strange.

20:33.023 --> 20:34.024
I was?

20:34.942 --> 20:37.153
What on earth did he say to her?

20:38.904 --> 20:42.241
He said something about you asking him
to be your husband.

20:42.867 --> 20:43.909
What?

20:43.993 --> 20:45.453
That fool.

20:45.536 --> 20:47.204
Did he tell her everything?

20:48.456 --> 20:50.624
We're really close, that's all.

20:51.208 --> 20:54.211
There's nothing we don't know
about each other.

20:54.712 --> 20:55.838
[chuckles nervously]

20:58.549 --> 21:00.968
Don't mind that at all.

21:01.635 --> 21:02.970
It was just a joke.

21:03.721 --> 21:05.556
Don't we all joke like that
every now and then?

21:05.639 --> 21:06.724
[♪ comical sting]

21:08.851 --> 21:11.103
[chuckles]
It's just my neighborhood, then.

21:11.187 --> 21:12.271
What?

21:13.564 --> 21:16.400
Did he say anything else?

21:16.484 --> 21:17.568
Like what?

21:18.944 --> 21:20.196
Never mind.

21:22.531 --> 21:25.284
MYUNGSOONDANG

21:28.662 --> 21:29.747
Thank you.

21:33.292 --> 21:35.127
He told me to watch myself.

21:35.211 --> 21:37.338
We should sign a non-disclosure agreement.

21:37.421 --> 21:40.758
What kind of guy
blabbers about everything?

21:44.720 --> 21:46.555
MYUNGSOONDANG PACKAGING DESIGN PROPOSAL

21:47.807 --> 21:50.059
As you can see,

21:50.142 --> 21:53.646
Myungsoondang's packaging
is usually simple and generic.

21:53.729 --> 21:56.315
So, on days other
than major national holidays,

21:56.398 --> 22:00.194
they seem a bit old-fashioned
for exams, Christmas, or birthdays.

22:02.988 --> 22:04.281
The new packaging

22:04.365 --> 22:06.909
caters to various special occasions
other than just national holidays

22:06.992 --> 22:09.954
with a more youthful, cute design.

22:10.037 --> 22:11.121
I like it.

22:11.205 --> 22:13.624
-That one over there is cute.
-They're pretty.

22:13.707 --> 22:15.084
It would be a Stargram hit.

22:17.920 --> 22:19.046
[remote beeps]

22:19.129 --> 22:20.256
Thank you.

22:20.881 --> 22:22.466
[all applauding]

22:23.342 --> 22:24.468
I like it.

22:25.803 --> 22:27.721
Wouldn't everyone want one?

22:27.805 --> 22:29.098
What do you think?

22:29.181 --> 22:30.182
It looks nice.

22:31.016 --> 22:33.018
-[Sejung] I really like the colors.
-[whispers] Good job.

22:33.102 --> 22:34.478
[Wonseok] This looks pretty cute.

22:35.271 --> 22:37.731
-Thank you.
-Well done.

22:41.151 --> 22:42.152
Mr. Kim.

22:44.697 --> 22:47.116
You young people
have such great ideas and taste.

22:47.199 --> 22:49.243
Thank you. I'll do my best.

22:49.326 --> 22:50.327
[chuckles softly]

22:51.370 --> 22:53.038
-Oh, Ms. Yoo.
-Yes?

22:53.122 --> 22:54.540
Are you free this evening?

22:55.708 --> 22:57.293
Well, yes.

22:57.376 --> 22:59.378
-[♪ whimsical music playing]
-Are your glasses filled?

23:00.546 --> 23:01.922
Okay, everyone.

23:02.006 --> 23:05.926
To the collaboration
of Myungsoondang and Merry Design Studio.

23:06.010 --> 23:07.720
-Cheers!
-[all] Cheers!

23:10.931 --> 23:12.474
[exclaims]

23:12.558 --> 23:13.934
Look at the marbling on the meat.

23:14.560 --> 23:16.228
Prime beef surely is better.

23:18.606 --> 23:20.107
Please enjoy, Mr. Kim.

23:20.190 --> 23:21.942
Yes, thank you.

23:22.026 --> 23:25.237
-You should eat, too, Sejung.
-I will. By the way...

23:25.321 --> 23:28.282
-Do you have a girlfriend?
-I don't.

23:28.866 --> 23:30.326
What about an ideal type?

23:31.911 --> 23:32.912
[Kim Wooju] Not really.

23:32.995 --> 23:34.330
Are you against marriage?

23:34.413 --> 23:39.627
No, I'm not against marriage,
but I don't think it's a must, either.

23:39.710 --> 23:40.836
[Wonseok] Hey.

23:40.920 --> 23:42.296
You and I are on the same page.

23:42.379 --> 23:45.257
I guess handsome guys think alike.

23:46.884 --> 23:49.887
Wonseok, you're not in his league.

23:50.512 --> 23:52.640
You're not single by choice.

23:52.723 --> 23:55.351
-You applied to be on I Am Single.
-[scoffs]

23:55.434 --> 23:56.727
-For real?
-I caught him

23:56.810 --> 23:58.646
-filling in the application form.
-[chuckles softly]

23:58.729 --> 24:00.606
You'll talk about anything.

24:00.689 --> 24:01.899
When will you be on the show?

24:01.982 --> 24:03.317
I heard the competition's fierce.

24:06.904 --> 24:08.906
Wait, they didn't call for an interview?

24:10.407 --> 24:13.035
-[bangs table]
-See? What did I tell you?

24:13.118 --> 24:16.830
If you want to get married,
you must go all in and buy an apartment.

24:16.914 --> 24:19.208
You still rent a place,
which is worse than losing hair.

24:19.291 --> 24:21.293
I told you to buy
the old apartment in Ojun-dong.

24:21.377 --> 24:23.462
It would've been great
if you'd bought it then.

24:23.545 --> 24:24.964
The value increased by 50 million won.

24:25.047 --> 24:26.173
[sighs]

24:27.299 --> 24:28.634
Okay.

24:28.717 --> 24:29.718
Let's drink.

24:29.802 --> 24:30.928
Sure.

24:32.763 --> 24:35.265
You can't afford a home
with a normal salary these days.

24:36.058 --> 24:37.393
I've given up in this lifetime.

24:37.476 --> 24:39.311
Where there's a will, there's a way.

24:39.395 --> 24:41.939
Why don't you enter
a department store raffle?

24:42.022 --> 24:43.649
They give away five-million-dollar places.

24:43.732 --> 24:45.651
[Wonseok] Five million dollars?
That's a thing?

24:45.985 --> 24:46.986
[Ms. Oh] You didn't know?

24:47.611 --> 24:48.737
Hang on. Is it over?

24:49.780 --> 24:51.490
It was Beauté Department Store.

24:51.949 --> 24:53.450
Beauté Department...

24:53.534 --> 24:54.785
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

24:56.829 --> 24:59.665
How about more beef? Korean beef.

24:59.748 --> 25:01.208
-Korean beef?
-Yes.

25:02.251 --> 25:03.585
Can you all eat some more?

25:04.294 --> 25:05.337
Yes, of course.

25:05.421 --> 25:07.715
[Ms. Oh exclaiming] Assorted special cuts?

25:08.507 --> 25:11.051
Neck chain, tri-tip, inside skirt...

25:11.802 --> 25:14.179
What do I do? Order them all?
It sounds so good.

25:14.263 --> 25:15.264
Excuse me!

25:15.347 --> 25:16.932
-Over here, ma'am.
-Yes?

25:19.268 --> 25:23.272
I heard about that raffle, too,
but I think it's over.

25:23.355 --> 25:24.773
They have announced the winner.

25:24.857 --> 25:26.316
Oh, hang on.

25:27.151 --> 25:28.485
Oh, Sejung.

25:28.569 --> 25:30.487
-Let's have a drink.
-Oh, okay.

25:31.155 --> 25:32.823
-Let's link arms.
-Us, you mean?

25:32.906 --> 25:34.366
Us, I mean.

25:34.450 --> 25:37.286
Hey, the winner was announced.

25:38.746 --> 25:42.291
The winners are Seoul residents, Yoo...

25:42.374 --> 25:43.542
[♪ dramatic music playing]

25:44.918 --> 25:47.004
Jaein and Kim Minseok.

25:47.087 --> 25:49.089
"They came to the store
to furnish their new home

25:49.173 --> 25:50.424
and happened to enter..."

25:50.507 --> 25:52.092
I'm jealous. [chuckles softly]

25:53.135 --> 25:54.136
Wait.

25:54.678 --> 25:57.598
Why do they look so familiar?

25:57.681 --> 25:58.682
These people...

25:59.183 --> 26:02.144
Ms. Oh, haven't we seen these people--

26:02.227 --> 26:05.397
Overcooked beef never tastes as good.

26:05.481 --> 26:06.565
Isn't it good?

26:06.982 --> 26:08.067
Oh, it's hot.

26:12.654 --> 26:16.742
Okay, everyone. If your glasses are empty,
I'll fill them for you.

26:16.825 --> 26:18.118
-Yes, sounds good.
-Sure.

26:21.955 --> 26:23.874
How about a group toast?

26:24.958 --> 26:26.251
-Okay.
-[all] Cheers!

26:26.335 --> 26:27.669
[cheering]

26:32.466 --> 26:33.842
It's so good.

26:39.681 --> 26:40.808
[sighs]

26:41.350 --> 26:42.476
I'm drunk.

26:43.936 --> 26:46.772
I can't be. I need to sober up.

26:49.274 --> 26:51.193
I need [hiccups] to stay alert.

26:52.778 --> 26:55.030
Ms. Yoo, are you all right?

26:55.114 --> 26:56.698
-You drank a lot.
-Yes. [hiccups]

26:56.782 --> 26:57.991
[slurring] I'm fine.

26:58.826 --> 27:00.828
I like seeing this side of you.

27:00.911 --> 27:03.622
You know I like people like you, right?

27:03.705 --> 27:05.624
[giggles] Thank you.

27:05.707 --> 27:07.417
[hiccups]

27:09.962 --> 27:11.296
You're paying, aren't you?

27:12.131 --> 27:14.174
-What?
-Our team leader's new to the job.

27:14.258 --> 27:15.467
Show your appreciation.

27:16.009 --> 27:17.970
Thanks for the Korean beef dinner.

27:18.053 --> 27:19.388
[♪ dramatic music playing]

27:19.763 --> 27:20.931
[acknowledges]

27:24.101 --> 27:26.019
I sobered up.

27:27.354 --> 27:28.397
[digital beeps]

27:28.480 --> 27:30.691
Oh, this card is overdrawn.

27:31.525 --> 27:32.568
Oh, then...

27:33.610 --> 27:34.611
Try this one.

27:35.320 --> 27:36.321
Okay.

27:37.489 --> 27:38.532
[digital beeps]

27:39.575 --> 27:40.868
This one, too.

27:42.828 --> 27:46.206
I paid the office rent yesterday.

27:46.290 --> 27:47.541
Give me a moment.

27:47.624 --> 27:49.001
-Sure.
-Another card...

27:49.710 --> 27:50.961
My other card...

27:51.044 --> 27:52.462
-Take your time.
-Okay.

27:54.590 --> 27:56.300
-[Kim Wooju] Put it on this one.
-Sure.

27:57.467 --> 27:59.553
I should pay for the dinner.

28:00.679 --> 28:02.014
[Ms. Oh] Mr. Kim.

28:03.390 --> 28:05.559
Ms. Yoo offered to pay today.

28:05.642 --> 28:08.145
Why should someone from another company
pay for our dinner?

28:08.228 --> 28:09.646
That's against company regulations.

28:09.730 --> 28:12.900
But Ms. Yoo insisted she'd pay.

28:14.443 --> 28:16.028
Thanks for the sentiment.

28:17.195 --> 28:18.906
Wait, Mr. Kim.

28:19.615 --> 28:20.908
The sentiment?

28:20.991 --> 28:22.701
I never offered anything.

28:22.784 --> 28:24.703
Excuse me? Mr. Kim!

28:27.789 --> 28:29.499
I'll head home.

28:29.583 --> 28:31.627
If anyone wants to stay out,
go have some fun.

28:31.710 --> 28:33.128
Thank you.

28:33.211 --> 28:36.006
[chuckles] Shall we go
to a karaoke, then?

28:36.089 --> 28:37.674
-Deal!
-Deal!

28:38.675 --> 28:40.052
Ms. Yoo.

28:40.135 --> 28:42.304
-You should come, too.
-Me?

28:42.387 --> 28:44.640
It looks like she had a lot to drink.

28:44.723 --> 28:47.476
[exclaims] It's no fun without her.

28:47.559 --> 28:49.853
-We're just getting started.
-Yes, let's go.

28:49.937 --> 28:51.146
No, I think...

28:51.647 --> 28:54.483
Where do you live? I'll drop you off.

28:54.566 --> 28:57.361
I live near...

28:57.444 --> 28:58.528
Get in.

28:58.612 --> 29:00.489
-[♪ comical music playing]
-I'll get in.

29:00.572 --> 29:01.740
Good. [chuckles nervously]

29:01.823 --> 29:04.201
We'll be going then.

29:04.284 --> 29:06.745
[Meri] Goodbye. Goodbye!

29:06.828 --> 29:07.829
[chuckles softly]

29:15.671 --> 29:16.672
[engine starts]

29:18.006 --> 29:19.383
[Wonseok] Goodbye!

29:19.466 --> 29:20.467
[Ms. Oh] What a shame.

29:21.176 --> 29:22.844
I was going to make her pay for karaoke.

29:30.936 --> 29:31.937
[groans softly]

29:32.562 --> 29:34.231
Karaoke.

29:34.314 --> 29:35.857
I wanted to go.

29:35.941 --> 29:38.235
Wash your feet and go to bed.

29:38.318 --> 29:39.820
I didn't want you to blurt anything out.

29:42.364 --> 29:43.699
"Blurt anything out"?

29:45.784 --> 29:49.955
He said something about you asking him
to be your husband.

29:50.038 --> 29:51.206
[snorts]

29:51.999 --> 29:53.917
You shouldn't go around saying things.

29:54.835 --> 29:56.211
What?

29:56.294 --> 29:58.672
I rarely make mistakes like that.

29:59.172 --> 30:01.216
Didn't you see me
refraining from drinking?

30:01.299 --> 30:03.969
You should be extra careful
when you're around others.

30:04.052 --> 30:06.388
Don't get me worried, too.

30:06.471 --> 30:08.765
You moved, right? Where is it?

30:11.601 --> 30:12.602
Are you asleep?

30:13.437 --> 30:16.148
Tell me where you live
before you doze off.

30:17.566 --> 30:18.567
Goodness.

30:23.780 --> 30:25.073
What the heck?

30:25.157 --> 30:27.826
Gosh, how much did she drink?

30:27.909 --> 30:29.911
DAEJONG MOTEL

30:29.995 --> 30:31.663
[♪ comical music continues]

30:47.971 --> 30:49.389
[grunts, panting]

30:49.473 --> 30:51.391
Try to walk, will you?

30:54.311 --> 30:57.189
-Which room is it?
-What?

30:57.272 --> 30:58.815
-This is it.
-This is the one?

30:58.899 --> 31:00.108
It's this room.

31:01.777 --> 31:03.070
Thank you.

31:03.153 --> 31:04.404
Sure. I'm off, then.

31:04.488 --> 31:06.156
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

31:07.199 --> 31:08.241
[pants]

31:13.121 --> 31:14.873
Where's my key card?

31:16.041 --> 31:17.042
Oh, dear.

31:18.126 --> 31:19.753
Where's my key card?

31:22.798 --> 31:25.634
-It was in here.
-Did you leave it in the room?

31:26.468 --> 31:27.511
[gasps]

31:27.969 --> 31:29.096
What do I do?

31:29.930 --> 31:32.182
-[sighs in exasperation]
-[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

31:32.682 --> 31:34.184
Jeez, this is the fifth floor.

31:38.647 --> 31:39.898
-I'll go downstairs.
-No.

31:39.981 --> 31:41.983
-I'll go.
-No, no.

31:42.067 --> 31:44.486
-Stay here. No, you stay.
-I can go.

31:44.569 --> 31:45.570
No, stay here.

31:45.654 --> 31:47.739
-I can--
-I prefer it this way.

31:47.823 --> 31:49.241
Watch your arm. Wait here.

31:49.324 --> 31:51.451
-Stay here.
-I can walk just fine.

31:51.535 --> 31:53.370
No, it's better if you stay here.

31:53.453 --> 31:54.955
-Here?
-Yes.

31:57.165 --> 31:58.166
[Meri mumbles]

31:58.667 --> 31:59.918
See you later.

32:01.837 --> 32:03.088
Just wait right there.

32:06.091 --> 32:07.425
[snoring]

32:09.678 --> 32:10.762
[beeping]

32:14.266 --> 32:15.267
You can go inside.

32:15.809 --> 32:17.144
Oh, thank you.

32:17.227 --> 32:19.271
She had a lot to drink.
[clears throat]

32:19.354 --> 32:20.438
Go inside.

32:21.064 --> 32:22.357
-[snoring]
-[Kim Wooju sighs]

32:23.900 --> 32:24.943
[grunts]

32:25.318 --> 32:26.903
Come along.

32:26.987 --> 32:29.406
-Come here. Get up.
-I'm sleepy.

32:29.489 --> 32:30.740
The door's open.

32:31.616 --> 32:33.994
[receptionist] Be sure
to take your key with you.

32:35.620 --> 32:36.872
[soft electrical hum]

32:36.955 --> 32:38.206
Easy now. Careful.

32:38.790 --> 32:39.833
[grunts]

32:40.792 --> 32:42.460
[slurs] Thank you.

32:42.544 --> 32:43.670
[panting]

32:47.007 --> 32:48.049
[sighs]

32:51.887 --> 32:52.929
[clears throat]

32:54.848 --> 32:57.767
Oh, I found it on the floor outside.

32:58.393 --> 32:59.519
[acknowledges]

33:00.020 --> 33:01.938
Oh, sure. Thanks.

33:06.443 --> 33:07.694
[♪ ominous sting]

33:07.777 --> 33:09.154
[♪ tense music playing]

33:12.616 --> 33:13.658
[gulps]

33:16.745 --> 33:19.247
Do you have anything else to say?

33:19.331 --> 33:20.498
Oh, no.

33:20.832 --> 33:21.833
Have a good night.

33:29.841 --> 33:30.926
[sighs in exasperation]

33:38.099 --> 33:39.142
[sighs]

33:48.235 --> 33:49.277
[gasps]

33:51.905 --> 33:53.365
You're leaving already?

33:53.448 --> 33:54.532
Yes.

33:56.618 --> 33:58.662
Oh, right. Room 203 wanted more towels.

34:07.170 --> 34:08.755
[♪ foreboding music playing]

34:17.055 --> 34:18.223
Goodbye.

34:21.851 --> 34:23.520
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

34:33.238 --> 34:34.531
[soft electrical hum]

35:09.941 --> 35:10.942
[exclaims]

35:11.026 --> 35:12.485
Easy now. Careful.

35:16.114 --> 35:17.407
CACTUS

35:18.658 --> 35:19.868
[line ringing]

35:20.869 --> 35:23.830
Hi, Ms. Yoo. Is my car key in your--

35:23.913 --> 35:25.040
[Meri screams]

35:28.585 --> 35:29.586
Ms. Yoo?

35:32.422 --> 35:33.715
[♪ ominous music playing]

35:47.854 --> 35:49.689
[♪ music crescendos]

35:50.649 --> 35:52.150
[♪ foreboding music playing]

35:53.735 --> 35:55.028
BE BACK SOON
PLEASE WAIT

36:04.162 --> 36:05.622
[panting]

36:16.966 --> 36:17.967
What's going on?

36:18.051 --> 36:19.386
[receptionist] Oh, you came back.

36:20.345 --> 36:21.388
[Meri screams]

36:23.264 --> 36:24.432
-Why--
-[Meri] Hold on.

36:25.350 --> 36:26.559
Are you all right?

36:27.519 --> 36:29.938
-[gasps] Oh, no.
-[receptionist] There's blood.

36:30.021 --> 36:31.231
I'm bleeding.

36:32.482 --> 36:33.566
[Meri] I'm sorry.

36:33.650 --> 36:35.360
Why did you punch him like that?

36:35.443 --> 36:36.695
What?

36:36.778 --> 36:38.238
He was touching your legs...

36:39.280 --> 36:40.490
[groans]

36:41.157 --> 36:42.534
It wasn't like that.

36:43.368 --> 36:46.913
I spilled my cup noodles
and burned my foot.

36:46.996 --> 36:49.624
He came by with a first-aid kit.

36:49.708 --> 36:51.084
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

36:51.167 --> 36:53.002
I'm so sorry, sir.

36:53.837 --> 36:55.130
-Oh, no.
-The blood won't stop.

36:55.213 --> 36:57.215
-You're still bleeding.
-What a mess.

36:57.298 --> 36:58.341
[receptionist crying]

36:58.425 --> 37:00.176
[Meri] Let's try to stop it with this.

37:02.011 --> 37:04.431
Well, I'm sorry.

37:07.600 --> 37:08.601
[groans softly]

37:10.311 --> 37:14.190
The rug needs cleaning,
so I docked it from your prepayment.

37:14.607 --> 37:16.067
-Just so you know.
-Okay.

37:17.444 --> 37:19.738
-I'm really sorry.
-[crying] Quit apologizing.

37:19.821 --> 37:22.240
Jeez, I can't believe my rotten luck.

37:24.909 --> 37:26.286
[continues crying]

37:26.870 --> 37:27.954
-Let's go.
-Okay.

37:28.037 --> 37:29.998
[receptionist] I think
I hurt my back, too.

37:30.081 --> 37:31.124
[Meri] I can manage.

37:38.089 --> 37:40.216
I didn't know you'd spilled something hot.

37:41.259 --> 37:43.386
Who eats cup noodles
when they're half-asleep?

37:43.470 --> 37:45.054
You had a huge dinner.

37:45.138 --> 37:46.765
I was hungry.

37:47.932 --> 37:51.352
I also wanted to eat beef,
but I didn't eat much because of the bill.

37:51.436 --> 37:53.772
So, I was too hungry to sleep.

37:55.774 --> 37:56.775
Sorry.

37:58.067 --> 37:59.444
[♪ gentle music playing]

38:02.572 --> 38:03.865
No, I'm sorry.

38:05.241 --> 38:07.368
I'm not angry with you.

38:08.953 --> 38:11.039
It's my circumstances that I can't stand.

38:12.707 --> 38:15.001
Stay at a hotel.

38:15.084 --> 38:17.796
Why scrimp when you'll soon
own a house worth millions?

38:17.879 --> 38:19.380
Spend when you must.

38:19.464 --> 38:21.800
I don't have the money
until the house is sold.

38:22.383 --> 38:24.093
It's not sold yet.

38:24.719 --> 38:27.555
I have an employee to pay
and a loan interest to cover.

38:28.056 --> 38:29.808
I can barely afford the office rent--

38:29.891 --> 38:30.975
[groans, sighs]

38:35.772 --> 38:37.398
[♪ dreamy, ambient music playing]

38:38.024 --> 38:39.234
[groans softly]

38:50.745 --> 38:52.831
Shouldn't you see a doctor?

38:52.914 --> 38:54.874
No, it's fine.

38:56.334 --> 38:57.335
Thank you.

38:59.838 --> 39:04.008
By the way, you pack a hefty punch.

39:04.759 --> 39:06.261
Just one gave him a nosebleed.

39:06.928 --> 39:09.013
[chuckles softly] That was nothing.

39:10.473 --> 39:14.060
But do you really not have
a place to spend the night?

39:14.143 --> 39:15.979
What about a friend or a relative?

39:17.605 --> 39:19.607
I don't know anyone in Seoul.

39:21.526 --> 39:26.030
It's fine. I'll just sleep
in my office for one night.

39:32.328 --> 39:33.329
Give me that.

39:33.955 --> 39:35.039
Where are we going?

39:35.123 --> 39:36.124
Follow me.

39:36.708 --> 39:38.084
[♪ feel-good music playing]

40:05.862 --> 40:07.447
-Give it to me.
-Just go up.

40:20.501 --> 40:22.170
Make sure he doesn't see you.

40:22.253 --> 40:24.756
I will. I'll be as quiet as a mouse.

40:24.839 --> 40:27.926
I'll go to work at dawn
and keep the lights off at night.

40:28.551 --> 40:29.552
Okay.

40:30.595 --> 40:31.596
Go on inside.

40:32.305 --> 40:33.640
[whispers] Bye. Thank you.

40:35.558 --> 40:36.643
[keypad beeping]

40:38.478 --> 40:40.438
Thanks. Drive safely.

40:42.565 --> 40:43.816
-[door closes, lock beeps]
-[sighs]

40:52.951 --> 40:54.118
[chuckles softly]

40:58.039 --> 40:59.499
Are you going home?

41:01.584 --> 41:03.086
You've been working late.

41:04.253 --> 41:06.172
The end of the quarter is always busy.

41:06.255 --> 41:08.216
You should take a break afterward.

41:08.299 --> 41:09.384
Of course.

41:09.467 --> 41:13.012
My son's upset with me,
so I'll take him fishing next weekend.

41:13.096 --> 41:14.138
[chuckling]

41:14.514 --> 41:15.765
Sounds good.

41:15.848 --> 41:17.225
Take this.

41:17.308 --> 41:20.436
The chairwoman gave it to me,
but I had too many already.

41:22.814 --> 41:24.232
-Thank you.
-Sure.

41:24.732 --> 41:25.817
[elevator dings]

41:27.068 --> 41:29.153
-Goodbye.
-Drive safely in the dark.

41:29.612 --> 41:30.613
Yes, sir.

41:42.709 --> 41:44.168
[♪ ominous music playing]

41:54.554 --> 41:56.014
[♪ foreboding music playing]

42:04.480 --> 42:05.481
[sighs softly]

42:31.007 --> 42:32.050
[engine starts]

42:47.940 --> 42:49.358
[♪ music increases in tempo]

42:53.446 --> 42:55.281
-[car horns blaring]
-[tires screech]

42:57.116 --> 42:58.117
[groans]

42:58.201 --> 42:59.535
What's wrong with me?
[clears throat]

43:01.704 --> 43:02.747
[car horn blares]

43:06.918 --> 43:08.795
-[tires screech]
-[truck horn blaring]

43:13.508 --> 43:14.550
[screams]

43:14.634 --> 43:15.885
[tires screeching]

43:26.354 --> 43:28.314
[♪ gripping, tense music swells, fades]

43:44.413 --> 43:45.665
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

43:46.457 --> 43:47.458
[sighs]

43:56.217 --> 43:58.052
[♪ soft melodious pop music playing]

44:15.862 --> 44:16.863
[yawns]

44:42.221 --> 44:43.347
[sighs deeply]

44:52.565 --> 44:53.649
[neck cracks]

44:56.110 --> 44:57.862
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

44:58.654 --> 44:59.780
Why won't he leave?

45:08.039 --> 45:09.707
Gosh, that was close.

45:11.667 --> 45:13.169
I should be careful.

45:15.004 --> 45:16.547
-An interview?
-[Sanghyeon] I scheduled it

45:16.631 --> 45:19.175
with an outlet to create an image
of connecting with young people.

45:20.259 --> 45:21.969
Here is the list of questions.

45:24.430 --> 45:26.349
Man, this game blows.

45:34.190 --> 45:38.319
"I visited the couple that won the house
with a housewarming gift."

45:38.402 --> 45:39.987
[scoffs] Who did?

45:40.488 --> 45:42.490
I did? When?

45:42.573 --> 45:44.533
You can drop by next weekend.

45:44.617 --> 45:45.910
We need it for PR.

45:47.328 --> 45:48.871
[sighs in exasperation]

45:48.955 --> 45:51.290
You're such a nuisance.

45:53.084 --> 45:54.085
Fine.

46:00.549 --> 46:01.550
Hey.

46:04.053 --> 46:05.513
Don't mess up this time.

46:10.351 --> 46:12.019
-Pardon?
-We lost an entire house

46:12.103 --> 46:13.604
because you messed up last time.

46:13.688 --> 46:15.356
I'm giving you another shot.

46:15.439 --> 46:16.440
Make up for it.

46:19.277 --> 46:20.278
Yes, sir.

46:20.695 --> 46:22.280
The CEO's visit?

46:22.363 --> 46:24.073
It's an unofficial visit.

46:24.156 --> 46:25.491
You don't have to worry.

46:25.825 --> 46:26.993
[hesitates]

46:27.410 --> 46:30.621
I need to discuss it with my husband.

46:31.455 --> 46:32.581
Yes.

46:34.041 --> 46:35.793
Okay, I understand.

46:36.836 --> 46:38.379
[♪ dramatic music playing]

46:40.131 --> 46:42.300
Why does he want to visit?

46:44.385 --> 46:45.428
[sighs wearily]

46:46.012 --> 46:47.013
[gasps]

46:48.931 --> 46:51.350
He didn't catch on, did he?

46:55.354 --> 46:57.565
No, right?

47:00.151 --> 47:01.652
What?

47:01.736 --> 47:03.070
Mr. Ko?

47:03.154 --> 47:04.864
He had been working late.

47:04.947 --> 47:06.574
He must have dozed off behind the wheel.

47:07.241 --> 47:08.367
[gasps softly]

47:10.161 --> 47:12.705
Which funeral hall is it? Ready my car.

47:12.788 --> 47:13.873
You'll go there now?

47:13.956 --> 47:16.584
I should. He worked for us for years.

47:17.668 --> 47:18.711
[gasps]

47:21.339 --> 47:22.548
[breathing heavily]

47:25.676 --> 47:27.136
You're not well.

47:27.219 --> 47:29.138
I'll go on my own today.

47:29.221 --> 47:30.765
Go home and rest.

47:30.848 --> 47:32.516
[breathing heavily]

47:34.477 --> 47:35.978
[♪ melancholy music playing]

48:01.420 --> 48:04.548
[Hangu] I don't know
what to say to console you.

48:05.132 --> 48:06.509
Please stay strong.

48:07.510 --> 48:10.137
Don't hesitate to contact me
if you need anything.

48:11.305 --> 48:12.723
[sniffling]

48:24.151 --> 48:26.237
[fitness instructor] Stand back up
and jog on the spot.

48:26.320 --> 48:28.948
Shake your wrists. One, two.

48:29.031 --> 48:30.825
Keep it light. Three, four.

48:30.908 --> 48:34.954
Kick your feet back. One, two, three.

48:35.037 --> 48:37.289
A bit faster now. One, two, three, four.

48:37.373 --> 48:39.333
Someone's passing to our left.

48:41.502 --> 48:42.503
Keep it up!

48:42.586 --> 48:45.589
-Keep going.
-Keep going.

48:52.680 --> 48:53.889
[Sungwoo] Hey, Sanghyeon.

48:53.973 --> 48:55.474
Don't mess up this time.

48:57.101 --> 49:01.230
Your home, your car,
your credit card, your VIP membership.

49:01.313 --> 49:03.566
I gave you all that to sort stuff out.

49:03.649 --> 49:04.942
Make yourself worthwhile.

49:05.776 --> 49:06.777
You can go now.

49:16.120 --> 49:17.496
[♪ dramatic music playing]

49:35.848 --> 49:37.016
[faucet running]

49:52.781 --> 49:53.782
[sighs]

49:59.079 --> 50:00.831
Oh, my gosh.

50:01.540 --> 50:03.667
How did people live
before they had electricity?

50:10.299 --> 50:11.300
[screams]

50:13.636 --> 50:14.845
My goodness.

50:16.555 --> 50:17.973
[♪ whimsical music playing]

50:29.652 --> 50:30.736
[bottle cap clatters]

50:31.403 --> 50:32.404
[sighs]

50:52.675 --> 50:53.759
[car alarm chirps]

51:06.981 --> 51:08.148
[hums softly]

51:09.483 --> 51:10.818
[mosquito buzzing]

51:15.197 --> 51:16.365
[mosquito buzzing]

51:16.949 --> 51:17.950
[exclaims softly]

51:20.411 --> 51:21.412
A mosquito?

51:21.704 --> 51:23.247
[persistent buzzing]

51:23.330 --> 51:24.582
[♪ whimsical music playing]

51:27.835 --> 51:28.836
[buzzing stops]

51:31.672 --> 51:32.673
[buzzing resumes]

51:35.759 --> 51:37.011
-[grunts]
-[buzzing stops]

51:38.679 --> 51:39.722
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

51:42.850 --> 51:44.518
[♪ tense whimsical music playing]

51:54.445 --> 51:55.529
What's going on?

52:20.137 --> 52:21.972
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

52:34.652 --> 52:35.944
[mumbles in frustration]

52:36.028 --> 52:37.196
[sighs in exasperation]

52:39.782 --> 52:40.866
[doorbell chimes]

52:43.952 --> 52:45.746
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

52:50.542 --> 52:51.752
[phone vibrating]

52:52.336 --> 52:54.046
MANAGING DIRECTOR BAEK

52:56.215 --> 52:57.591
[phone continues vibrating]

53:07.976 --> 53:08.977
[Sanghyeon chuckles softly]

53:09.061 --> 53:11.397
I had something to give you,
and you seemed to be home.

53:12.439 --> 53:13.607
It's a parking permit form.

53:13.691 --> 53:16.151
You haven't registered your car yet.

53:16.235 --> 53:18.987
Thanks, I'll fill it in
and take it to the management office.

53:20.864 --> 53:22.574
Do you know...

53:23.492 --> 53:26.787
if I can ask the management office
to fix my lights?

53:26.870 --> 53:28.414
Is there a problem?

53:28.497 --> 53:32.626
The lights go on and off
on their own for no reason.

53:33.961 --> 53:35.212
[exclaims in realization]

53:36.130 --> 53:38.882
Did you activate the audio sensor?

53:39.508 --> 53:40.551
Who, me?

53:54.982 --> 53:56.817
-[gasps softly]
-[♪ enchanting music playing]

53:59.445 --> 54:03.449
You can clap to control the lights
in the living room and each bedroom.

54:03.532 --> 54:05.325
To deactivate the audio sensor...

54:06.827 --> 54:08.412
[beeps] press "deactivate."

54:08.787 --> 54:10.164
[exclaims in realization]

54:11.498 --> 54:13.250
-Let's try it in the living room.
-Okay.

54:19.923 --> 54:23.552
This is pretty useful when you're too lazy
to go upstairs to get the lights.

54:23.635 --> 54:25.596
Press the button for the second floor
[beeps]

54:25.679 --> 54:27.347
and clap.

54:29.808 --> 54:31.685
You can control the upstairs lights, too.

54:32.686 --> 54:36.273
I guess your husband isn't home yet.

54:38.275 --> 54:39.276
Overtime.

54:40.027 --> 54:43.363
Yes, he works overtime almost every day.

54:43.447 --> 54:45.491
What does he do
if you don't mind me asking?

54:46.450 --> 54:47.534
[hesitates]

54:48.452 --> 54:50.120
He's an ordinary...

54:50.746 --> 54:52.915
He works at an ordinary company.

54:53.332 --> 54:54.458
[acknowledges]

54:54.791 --> 54:55.834
[inhales sharply]

54:56.251 --> 55:01.590
Does your husband actually live here?

55:02.090 --> 55:03.675
-Yes, why?
-[♪ tense whimsical music playing]

55:03.759 --> 55:05.427
I never see him around.

55:05.511 --> 55:07.346
His car's not in the parking lot,

55:07.846 --> 55:11.475
and I don't see his items
anywhere in the house.

55:15.187 --> 55:17.689
The bedroom was full of your things.

55:26.323 --> 55:29.201
And in the hallway, I only saw your shoes.

55:30.118 --> 55:32.162
There's no trace of your husband.

55:32.246 --> 55:33.956
It's as if you live apart.

55:38.585 --> 55:40.420
So, my husband's...

55:40.504 --> 55:42.631
His stuff is all upstairs.

55:43.298 --> 55:46.093
We need to unpack, but we're too busy.

55:46.760 --> 55:48.762
We should do that this weekend.

55:53.183 --> 55:54.268
[chuckles nervously]

55:55.769 --> 55:56.770
I see.

55:57.229 --> 55:58.397
Yes.

55:58.480 --> 55:59.565
[Meri chuckles]

55:59.982 --> 56:01.984
Then I'll give you time to unpack.

56:03.277 --> 56:05.737
Can our CEO visit next week?

56:06.822 --> 56:07.823
Next week?

56:10.117 --> 56:11.451
Next week...

56:12.911 --> 56:14.538
[♪ jazz music playing over stereo]

56:17.583 --> 56:19.918
-[phone vibrates]
-[clears throat]

56:22.212 --> 56:26.008
[Meri] Do you have
any spare trainers or clothes?

56:26.091 --> 56:27.217
What does this mean?

56:30.470 --> 56:31.471
[music stops]

56:32.431 --> 56:33.473
[line ringing]

56:34.975 --> 56:35.976
Hello?

56:36.893 --> 56:41.732
Well, I think I need to keep
some of your stuff at the house.

56:41.815 --> 56:44.109
The CEO wants to visit.

56:44.693 --> 56:46.361
What? The CEO?

56:47.070 --> 56:49.197
I couldn't say no.

56:49.281 --> 56:52.701
Mr. Baek was over, and he suspected us.

56:52.784 --> 56:54.828
Mr. Baek was there?

56:54.911 --> 56:55.912
What for?

56:56.663 --> 56:58.040
[♪ whimsical music playing]

56:59.374 --> 57:00.375
What?

57:01.585 --> 57:03.712
Why did you try to kill the mosquito?

57:03.795 --> 57:05.088
So what if you get bitten?

57:05.172 --> 57:06.256
Would it kill you?

57:06.340 --> 57:08.800
That's a matter of willpower.

57:08.884 --> 57:10.594
When I was at Boy Scout camp,

57:10.677 --> 57:12.512
I didn't complain
when I got bitten 20 times.

57:12.596 --> 57:13.972
"I'll die if I get caught."

57:14.056 --> 57:15.766
You should've put up with it.

57:15.849 --> 57:18.268
Who can ignore a mosquito?

57:18.352 --> 57:19.686
A fly, maybe.

57:19.770 --> 57:21.146
Learn to put up with both.

57:21.229 --> 57:23.649
You need to steel yourself
if you want to pull off a scam.

57:23.732 --> 57:25.692
How will you manage
with a mindset like that?

57:26.610 --> 57:27.986
Okay.

57:28.987 --> 57:29.988
[clears throat]

57:31.448 --> 57:33.950
When will the CEO visit?

57:34.910 --> 57:35.911
Will you come?

57:38.538 --> 57:39.790
[people chattering]

57:49.758 --> 57:51.009
[both giggle]

57:54.471 --> 57:55.555
[sighs]

58:01.645 --> 58:02.688
[sniffles]

58:08.527 --> 58:10.237
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

58:10.320 --> 58:11.988
[♪ dreamy, ethereal music playing]

58:39.015 --> 58:41.393
I didn't think
wedding photos would be necessary.

58:42.144 --> 58:45.230
What newlywed couple
doesn't have one on the wall?

58:45.313 --> 58:46.606
That's true, but...

58:46.690 --> 58:49.317
I could also get into trouble
if you're caught.

58:49.401 --> 58:50.569
[acknowledges]

58:50.902 --> 58:51.903
Here.

58:52.571 --> 58:53.572
[gasps softly]

58:55.824 --> 58:56.825
They're plastic.

58:56.908 --> 58:58.452
-I found them over there.
-[chuckles softly]

58:58.535 --> 58:59.661
I see.

58:59.745 --> 59:01.913
-Shall we begin?
-Yes, then...

59:01.997 --> 59:04.499
Will you sit over there?
I'll stand next to you.

59:04.583 --> 59:05.584
Okay.

59:08.044 --> 59:09.171
[sighs]

59:13.633 --> 59:14.760
[inhales sharply]

59:15.844 --> 59:16.887
[exclaims]

59:16.970 --> 59:19.598
None of the dresses fit me right.

59:19.681 --> 59:21.475
I can barely breathe.

59:22.893 --> 59:24.019
[clears throat]

59:25.187 --> 59:26.605
-Excuse me.
-What?

59:26.688 --> 59:28.231
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

59:28.774 --> 59:29.775
Do you feel better?

59:30.650 --> 59:31.651
Yes.

59:36.865 --> 59:37.949
[Meri clears throat]

59:42.662 --> 59:45.290
If we have to feel uneasy anyway,
we might as well do it properly.

59:45.373 --> 59:47.250
A half-baked job will only get us caught.

59:47.334 --> 59:48.418
[Meri acknowledges]

59:49.377 --> 59:52.756
Then if you don't mind...

59:59.513 --> 01:00:00.764
Move closer.

01:00:03.391 --> 01:00:04.601
[soft, pulsing heartbeat]

01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:13.735
[Meri] What's wrong with you, Meri?

01:00:13.819 --> 01:00:16.822
Do you think these are
your actual wedding photos?

01:00:19.991 --> 01:00:21.243
[Kim Wooju clears throat]

01:00:21.326 --> 01:00:22.911
-Are you ready?
-Yes.

01:00:24.538 --> 01:00:25.956
[camera timer beeping]

01:00:26.832 --> 01:00:28.375
One, two, three.

01:00:32.629 --> 01:00:34.214
I'm a bit puffy today.

01:00:34.297 --> 01:00:35.298
-Hey.
-Face, check.

01:00:35.382 --> 01:00:36.758
I'm extra cute today.

01:00:36.842 --> 01:00:38.051
What am I going to do?

01:00:38.134 --> 01:00:40.428
-Guys!
-Sejung's here.

01:00:40.512 --> 01:00:42.180
Let's take some awesome photos today.

01:00:42.264 --> 01:00:43.807
-Sounds good.
-How should we pose?

01:00:43.890 --> 01:00:45.058
-What do you want?
-A sexy look?

01:00:45.141 --> 01:00:46.226
-Okay.
-That's my specialty.

01:00:46.309 --> 01:00:47.644
One, two, three.

01:00:48.562 --> 01:00:50.272
-We're friends just for today.
-Perfect.

01:00:50.355 --> 01:00:52.566
-Just for today.
-Just for today.

01:00:52.649 --> 01:00:53.984
[chuckling]

01:00:56.403 --> 01:00:57.404
That was great.

01:00:57.487 --> 01:00:58.905
-Good.
-Let's go.

01:01:02.158 --> 01:01:03.285
[chuckles nervously]

01:01:09.040 --> 01:01:11.418
I think that will do it.

01:01:15.130 --> 01:01:16.798
[♪ dreamy, ambient music playing]

01:01:18.884 --> 01:01:19.926
[exclaims softly]

01:01:22.178 --> 01:01:23.930
Get changed. I'll see you outside.

01:01:24.014 --> 01:01:25.015
Okay.

01:01:26.725 --> 01:01:27.893
[door opens]

01:01:28.852 --> 01:01:30.103
-[sighs softly]
-[door closes]

01:01:34.024 --> 01:01:35.150
[sighs]

01:01:44.576 --> 01:01:46.786
[Sejung's friend 1] Sejung,
did you bring those shades?

01:01:46.870 --> 01:01:49.706
[Sejung] Yes,
shouldn't you come prepared?

01:01:49.789 --> 01:01:51.583
You're such a thoughtful planner.

01:01:51.666 --> 01:01:53.043
[♪ dramatic sting]

01:01:53.126 --> 01:01:55.003
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

01:01:56.004 --> 01:01:57.255
Mr. Kim?

01:01:57.339 --> 01:01:58.381
[Sejung's friend 2] What?

01:01:58.465 --> 01:02:00.550
I think I just saw someone I know.

01:02:00.634 --> 01:02:01.801
[Sejung's friend 2] Who?

01:02:01.885 --> 01:02:02.886
[Sejung] My team leader.

01:02:05.889 --> 01:02:07.515
-Hang on.
-Why?

01:02:08.475 --> 01:02:09.809
-What? We're going back in?
-Hurry.

01:02:09.893 --> 01:02:10.894
Why?

01:02:15.649 --> 01:02:17.233
-Out there...
-Yes?

01:02:17.317 --> 01:02:18.485
Sejung's here.

01:02:18.568 --> 01:02:19.569
What?

01:02:21.321 --> 01:02:22.739
Where did he go?

01:02:22.822 --> 01:02:24.324
Shouldn't you say hi?

01:02:24.407 --> 01:02:25.617
I should, right?

01:02:25.700 --> 01:02:27.077
Why would you do that?

01:02:27.160 --> 01:02:28.912
Hey, is he good-looking?

01:02:28.995 --> 01:02:29.996
Hey.

01:02:30.789 --> 01:02:32.624
Hurry up, then. I want to meet him.

01:02:32.707 --> 01:02:34.793
-Hello? Mr. Kim?
-Open all the rooms.

01:02:34.876 --> 01:02:36.544
What now? What do we do?

01:02:36.628 --> 01:02:39.422
-Let's...
-There's nowhere to hide.

01:02:49.140 --> 01:02:50.350
Sorry for this.

01:02:53.520 --> 01:02:55.355
[♪ dreamy, ambient music playing]

01:03:01.861 --> 01:03:03.405
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

01:03:11.913 --> 01:03:13.331
Mr. Kim?

01:03:14.624 --> 01:03:15.625
[gasps softly]

01:03:16.668 --> 01:03:17.711
[gasps]

01:03:36.104 --> 01:03:37.397
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

01:04:03.548 --> 01:04:06.217
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:04:06.301 --> 01:04:08.470
[Meri] Don't you know
offense is the best defense?

01:04:08.553 --> 01:04:10.472
He was clearly suspicious last time.

01:04:10.555 --> 01:04:13.391
[Sanghyeon] Unsolicited words of comfort
are just arrogance.

01:04:13.475 --> 01:04:14.476
[Kim Wooju] Baek Sanghyeon?

01:04:15.143 --> 01:04:16.436
[Hangu] Team Leader Kim?

01:04:16.519 --> 01:04:18.146
[Kim Wooju] Why do you need to change?

01:04:18.229 --> 01:04:21.649
You'll meet someone
who won't take your love for granted.

01:04:21.733 --> 01:04:24.360
You liar.

01:04:24.444 --> 01:04:26.571
My mom's in Seoul and heading to Wooju's.

01:04:26.654 --> 01:04:28.114
[Wooju's mom] This isn't a lovers' spat.

01:04:28.198 --> 01:04:29.199
It's over between them.

01:04:29.282 --> 01:04:30.366
[Kim Wooju] Don't worry.

01:04:30.450 --> 01:04:33.244
I think she's ready
to hear your side of the story.

01:04:33.328 --> 01:04:34.329
[Wooju] Yoo Meri.

01:04:35.121 --> 01:04:36.122
Kim Wooju.

01:04:39.542 --> 01:04:41.544
Translated by Jennifer Jean Lim
